      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The accuracy of assessments of Type A behaviour made using different methods is the focus of active debate. Presented here are preliminary meta-analyses regarding: (a) internal consistency, test-retest and parallel forms reliabilities of the most frequently used questionnaire (Jenkins Activity Survey); (b) inter-rater and test-retest reliabilities of the most prospectively valid method (Friedman Structured Interview); and (c) correlations and percentage classification agreement between these measures. The findings generally suggest highly statistically significant yet moderate effect strengths for these various psychometric properties."},
